1 |\n507|| execdeps (lifecycle.go:Execute) | B36 nil-lifecycle pinned; singleton arms | B36 nil-lifecycle pinned; singleton arms | B36 nil-lifecycle pinned; singleton arms | B36 nil-lifecycle pinned; singleton arms | B36 nil-lifecycle pinned; singleton arms | B36 nil-lifecycle pinned; singleton arms | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 | U1 |\n508|\n509|Symmetry (every gate on two or more sides, with admitting-row\n510|counts per side; \"shared\" marks one row killing through several\n511|entries, attribution verified per entry from the raw logs):\n512|directive CMD 1 / PDIR 1 shared; scrub OSR 2 / UNT 2 shared; cmdident\n513|CMD 3 members; cmdvector EXC 1 / EXA 1 / EXE 1 / EXR 1 / CMD 4;\n514|directives 6 EX + DIRV shared 1; effectvocab/exitrefused/transport\n515|single-sided at PFX; reconfirm/escalation/persistmap/attachmap\n516|single-sided at PFX; boundarywait EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; staterecord\n517|REC 2 members; statelookup LOOK 2 members; entrypoint/transportvocab\n518|single-sided at UNT; absentmemory EXS 1 / CLS 1 shared; presentmemory\n519|EXS 1 / CLS 1 / OBSP 1 shared; attachable EXS 1 / CLS 1 shared; cutrow\n520|OBSP 1 / UNT 1 shared (EXS B23); triple EXS 1 / UNT 1 shared; dialstale\n521|DIAL 2 members; probedeps PRB 2 members; sunpath LEN 1 / 6 EX 1 /\n522|PRB 1 shared; placement CUS 1 / PRB 1 shared; leafdelegate CUS 1 (B32\n523|propagation elsewhere); leafwiring CUS 2 sites; rootwrite CUS 1 /\n524|EXC 1 / EXS 1 / EXR 1 / shared EachOperation row (EXA, EXE, EXT);\n525|ancestorwrite CUS 1 / EXS 1 / EXR 1 / shared EachOperation row\n526|(EXC, EXA, EXE, EXT); socketkind CUS 1 / shared EachOperation row\n527|(6 EX); ancestorkind CUS 1 /\n528|PRB 1 / SPW 1 shared; backendid 6 EX shared 1; agreement EXC 4\n529|members; enginemembers EXE 4 members; attachcap EXA 2 members;\n530|attestation EXA 1 + pinned member; authkind EXT 2 / EXR 2; generation\n531|EXT 1 / EXR 2; deadline EXA 1 / EXT 1 / EXR 2; keymaterial EXT 1 / EXR\n532|1; capdual EXT 2 members; fencingmap EXT 2 + 3 pinned; target EXT 3\n533|members; winner EXT 2 members (session arm U3: fencing+target\n534|precede); record EXT 1 / EXR 1 shared + UNT 1; replay EXT 2 + 6\n535|pinned; bindmap/bindfound single-sided at EXT; readonly EXA 1 / CMD 1\n536|shared; detachvec CMD 1; boundarykind/boundexit EXE 1 each + PFX\n537|0/1; quiescedetach EXE 1 / PFX 1 shared; nosendkeys/closeexit EXE 1\n538|each; probemarker EXS 1 / EXE 1 / EXT 1 shared; probeneg EXE 1;\n539|identity CUS 1; bindcontract/restoreagree EXR 1 each; replaytime EXE\n540|2; after-restore outcomes in Table E (launch/reattach/offer/park/\n541|refuse + refresh audit); outcomekey REC 1 / LOOK 1; binddocid REC\n542|1 / LOOK 1; binddocshape REC 1; docpersist EXR 1; attachreadonly\n543|EXA 1; quiescereport/boundaryreport EXE 3 rows each\n544|(corrupt/empty/crash legs); statusunbound/statusdoc/statusmatch/\n545|statusnegative EXS 1 each + statusmatch LOOK 1; prioragree EXR 4\n546|tests, 3 rows; succession EXR 3 members; execdeps 6 EX pinned\n547|(B36); Table B verify 9 new-entry sides shared 1, server EXA 1 (its\n548|other sides are first-leaf symmetry).\n549|\n550|Ratio: 227 measured of 5576 (50+10+167 M across Tables A/B/D;\n551|Table C all U); 156 bound; 4193 unreachable with reasons. Every\n552|driven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 27\n553|driven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\n554|B29 poll past-deadline, B32 propagation, B36 singleton deps) and\n555|125 named undriven gaps (B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch\n556|side, and the 117 B39 reachable-undriven cells), each with its\n557|owner below. (Table A's 4 B15 guard-name arms are bound outside\n558|this split.)\n559|\n560|Table E: after-restore outcome grid (ExecuteWrapperRestore,\n561|wrapper.go:97). Each row is one decided outcome with its evidence\n562|condition, its backend effect, and the committed test plus the\n563|narrowing row that kills a routing/order mutant through the\n564|wrapper entry (test names drop the Test prefix):\n565|\n566|| Outcome | Evidence condition | Backend effect | Test / row |\n567||---|---|---|---|\n568|| launch | verified local win + valid materialization | executes backend restore exactly once | WrapperRestoreLocalWinResumes; reorder covered by N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n569|| reattach | verified local win + recorded bootstrap pair | executes backend restore exactly once | WrapperRestoreReattachReplaysBackend; reorder covered by N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n570|| attach_remote | refreshed remote winner + lapsed local grant + interactive | none (no backend op, no exec, no provider) | WrapperRestoreLapsedGrantRemoteOffer/attach; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n571|| takeover_offer | refreshed remote winner + lapsed local grant + non-capable attach | none (no backend op, no exec, no provider) | WrapperRestoreLapsedGrantRemoteOffer/takeover; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n572|| parked (remote-noninteractive) | refreshed remote winner + non-interactive terminal | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/remote-noninteractive; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n573|| parked (refresh-failed) | refresh error → unverified local knowledge | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/refresh-failed; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n574|| parked (no-adapter) | missing refresh adapter → unverified local knowledge | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/no-adapter; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n575|| parked (no-known-lease) | no lease known at all → zero winner | none | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/no-known-lease; N-wrapper-reorder-refresh |\n576|| parked (invalid-material) | required materialization not admitted | none (routing mutant would execute) | WrapperRestoreParksWithoutEffects/invalid-material; N-wrapper-route-material |\n577|| parked (refresh-timeout) | refresh blocks → cancelled at the bound, unverified | none | WrapperRestoreRefreshBoundMeasured/configured-50ms; N-refresh-bound-default (default leg) |\n578|| refuse (mode) | Decide.Mode != restore (incl. garbage) | none, invalid-arguments | WrapperRestoreRefusesMalformed; N-wrapper-mode |\n579|| refuse (operation) | Restore.Operation != restore (incl. garbage) | none, invalid-arguments | WrapperRestoreRefusesMalformed; N-wrapper-operation |\n580|| refuse (deps) | nil lifecycle or nil dependency | none, protocol-error | WrapperRestoreRefusesMalformed; B36 singleton (no narrowing row) |\n581|\n582|The refresh runs before the decision on every row (N-wrapper-\n583|reorder-refresh admits exactly the fixture session past the\n584|refresh-success arm into stale local knowledge and is killed by\n585|the offer/resume/park tests together), so the offer path never\n586|presents the lapsed grant to backend restore authorization.\n587|Union-rival ambiguity is unmodeled (B38). The parked wire result\n588|of the backend restore entry itself (RestoredParked) stays a\n589|backend-row concern, not a Table E row.\n590|\n591|## Stated bounds\n(more lines below)","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
