{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000db2d","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c7e8-b0ce-7b51-a856-c1e5aeba35b8"},"sequence":3057,"recorded_at":1780531400006109,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419"},"call_id":"call_01a0c7fc03ff73ae896b08b7046faf74","text":"Read text file `internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`.\n(590 line(s) above)\n591|## Stated bounds\n592|\n593|- B1 Determinism: no row has a real-tmux witness. Every broker, server,\n594|  and spawner interaction runs through injected dependencies; the suite\n595|  passes with no tmux process anywhere. A live-server test would add a\n596|  witness, not a rule, and is sibling scope.\n597|- B2 Windows refusal: native Windows MUST NOT claim tmux (pinned SPEC\n598|  1458). The Windows platform refuses at the lexical gate on every host\n599|  (row 15); the Windows commit/verify arms refuse every platform and\n600|  exist only so the package compiles under GOOS=windows.\n601|- B3 Nil-dependency weakening on the foreground path panics instead of\n602|  misbehaving; the narrowing row pins the refusal and discloses the\n603|  panic kill.\n604|- B4 No gate inspects source text, so no token-preserving mutant\n605|  applies; the harness executes the behavioral suite.\n606|- B5 Attach presentation vectors are sibling scope: attached and broker\n607|  outcomes carry the socket, and only the spawned outcome carries argv.\n608|- B6 Lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, stop,\n609|  terminate, restore) belong to the sibling leaves, not to acquisition.\n610|- B7 The handle-mismatch arm stages its race through the sameDirectory\n611|  seam; a true concurrent handle swap is not staged.\n612|- B8 Registry bindings and the digest re-pin belong to the story's\n613|  final leaf; this leaf documents clause coverage here and in the\n614|  conformance matrix only.\n615|- B9 Adapter split: this leaf ships the decision core and argv only. No\n616|  production probe or spawner implementation exists in the tree; the\n617|  exec/probe adapters that report Reconcile/ResolveEvidence verdicts\n618|  and spawn through the built argv, and the server socket's crash\n619|  evidence, are owned by the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz. The\n620|  no-fallback proof covers spawns routed through Dependencies.Spawn;\n621|  a fallback through a direct os/exec call is excluded today only by\n622|  the import census (no os/exec import in the package).\n623|  Dependencies.Spawn is inert on the background path: a nil spawner\n624|  with a live broker still contacts (the broker path never calls it),\n625|  so the field is dead weight there — which is what makes the\n626|  shared-Dependencies fallback shape realistic, and why the spy\n627|  census arms the foreground probe alongside the spawner.\n628|- B10 Crash convergence assumes a umask that preserves owner rwx\n629|  (umask & 0700 == 0). Under an owner-bit-stripping umask a leaf\n630|  stranded between mkdirat and the explicit chmod refuses on retry\n631|  instead of converging, because existing leaves verify, never repair.\n632|- B11 A symlinked intermediate component inside the root path is\n633|  followed; only the root's last component refuses (row 9). This\n634|  matches the landed secprim root open and is the same bound.\n635|- B12 The landed argv shape refusal (BuildArgv via secprim.CheckArgv)\n636|  is reachable only by direct call with a non-filesystem runtime dir\n637|  (witnessed by TestBuildArgvRefusesInvalidArgvShape); through Acquire\n638|  the directory always names a created directory.\n639|- B13 Sentinel/smoke sufficiency, signature verification, liveness,\n640|  and expiry are the landed Reconcile admission's verdict, consumed\n641|  here through Has. This leaf decides membership plus generation\n642|  binding only; the host-binding and provider-build cross-bind the\n643|  wrapper evaluates stays with the lifecycle owner.\n644|- B14 The battery and the read-only-root test assume a non-root test\n645|  user: N-fchmod-umask admits non-root creates past the explicit\n646|  chmod, so under root it is equivalent to the original and survives,\n647|  and TestEnsureRuntimeDirRefusesReadOnlyRoot stages a genuine EACCES\n648|  only when permission bits bind the test user. The reviewer's\n649|  same-shaped plant carries the identical assumption.\n650|- B15 Unmeasured fail-closed stat arms, no seam: handleBoundToPath's\n651|  two stat-failure arms (runtime.go) and verifyOwnership's !ok arm\n652|  (ownership_unix.go) fail closed by code and are prose only by test —\n653|  no test can stage a Stat failure on an open directory handle, or a\n654|  stat without ownership metadata on unix, without a seam. The\n655|  guard.Resolve refusal arm (runtime.go) is unreachable through the\n656|  name grammar: every input the guard would refuse is refused earlier\n657|  by scalar, so the fail-open plant survives by construction. The\n658|  secprim.NewGuard refusal arm (runtime.go:94-96) is the same class:\n659|  no committed input reaches it. The same unstageable class covers\n660|  the commit-side Fchmod and parent-Fsync failure arms and the\n661|  commit-side (runtime_unix.go:76-79) and verify-side leaf-Stat\n662|  failure arms: no committed test stages those failures. An\n663|  unopenable (0000) root reports `runtime containment` on both entries\n664|  with no committed test staging it — classifying EACCES as missing\n665|  would reroute it to `runtime root`, refusal-to-refusal. Reported\n666|  as error-arm rows, never counted among the narrowing survivors.\n667|- B16 The collision gate compares cleaned byte strings: an ambient\n668|  value naming the derived socket through a symlinked or relative\n669|  alias of the root walks past it (realpath equivalence is not\n670|  applied, and a cwd-relative spelling never equals the absolute\n671|  derived socket). Roots containing a comma are outside the TMUX\n672|  member's encoding: the gate splits at the first comma exactly as\n673|  tmux(1) itself does, so a comma-root socket component walks past\n674|  it. The spec rule is unaffected — the socket is derived, never\n675|  selected from an ambient value — so this bounds only the\n676|  package-local defense-in-depth claim. An `ax` invocation from\n677|  inside its own AX pane refuses `ambient collision` when the caller\n678|  populates Ambient from the process environment\n679|  (TMUX=`<derived>`,pid,idx in the real encoding): over-strict\n680|  rather than over-permissive, and the caller owns what it observes\n681|  — the lifecycle leaf TASK-260830-1c28dz decides the\n682|  nested-invocation rule deliberately.\n683|- B17 The mode gate reads permission bits only: setgid/sticky bits on\n684|  a 0700 leaf are admitted and macOS ACLs are not inspected. This\n685|  matches the landed hosttrust custody precedent\n686|  (internal/hosttrust/custody_unix.go platformModeOK: Perm() == mode),\n687|  so it is the same bound, not a fork.\n688|- B18 The derived socket path is not checked against the platform\n689|  sun_path limit (104 bytes on macOS); a deep runtime root surfaces\n690|  as a spawn failure in the lifecycle leaf's adapter, owned by\n691|  TASK-260830-1c28dz.\n692|- B19 The Runtime IPC root's own mode and ownership are not gated in\n693|  this leaf: the root arrives as the caller-supplied\n694|  localstore-resolved PathRuntime value, its creation-time custody is\n695|  the localstore layout owner's, and the SPEC 810-812\n696|  before-bind/connect rejection of an unsafe path, parent, or ancestor\n697|  is the lifecycle bind step's (TASK-260830-1c28dz), which is the step\n698|  that binds. This leaf pins the root handle (no-follow open plus\n699|  handle/path binding) and commits the leaf relative to it; a\n700|  world-writable root is admitted here and refused at bind. That the\n701|  root value is the landed localstore PathRuntime is a contract\n702|  statement about the caller, not a driven fact: no test composes\n703|  localstore with Acquire.\n704|- B20 Whether the runtime leaf was created by AX is indistinguishable\n705|  after the fact: any same-user 0700 directory under an admitted name\n706|  is accepted. The verifiable properties — mode, ownership, kind,\n707|  containment — are gated (rows 1-15); provenance is not claimed.\n708|- B21 No broker is modelled as the zero BrokerReport, whose\n709|  Principal.UID is 0: for a non-root process the absent broker\n710|  refuses on the authentication arm, while under a root process the\n711|  same-user arm passes and refusal comes from the generation arm.\n712|  The broker-path outcome socket binding is the generation equality\n713|  only — BrokerReport carries no socket of its own.\n714|- B22 Singleton arms ship no narrowing mutant: admitting the\n715|  singleton refused member is deleting the gate. Covered sites, each\n716|  test-pinned in both directions where a fork exists: create relay\n717|  transport (relay), descriptor presence fork (descpresence),\n718|  attach admission nil (serveadmitnil), spawner runner nil\n719|  (spawnnil), reconcile verifier nil (reconcilenil), states root\n720|  empty (stateopen), persist/attach stores nil (storenil),\n721|  failed-kill self-confirm (selfconfirm), and live-after-escalation\n722|  (stoptimeout). The outcome-lookup empty-key arm left this bound:\n723|  it narrows now (LookupOutcomeRefusesForgedKey /\n724|  N-outcome-key-forged). Owner: this leaf; retest if any site\n725|  grows a second refused member.\n726|- B23 The landed status engine normalizes backend error details to\n727|  \"status observation unknown\" (coded or not), so the cutrow and\n728|  empty-panes narrowings measure at the helper entries while the\n729|  dispatch legs pin the code. Owner: this leaf; retest if the\n730|  engine stops normalizing.\n731|- B24 The idempotency-store Completed read-failure arm is unstaged:\n732|  no seam fails receipt reads (hooks fire on write paths only).\n733|  Owner: hardening; stage with a read-failure seam to measure.\n734|- B25 The Bind clean-miss sub-arm is unstageable: every Bind error\n735|  the hooks stage leaves the committed file, so Lookup always finds\n736|  it. The clean-found sub-arm is measured (N-bind-hook-found).\n737|  Owner: hardening.\n738|- B26 The attach effect-failure dispatch mapping is unstaged: no\n739|  committed failure reaches it (the store replays identical\n740|  receipts; conflicting receipts are untested at dispatch).\n741|  Owner: hardening.\n742|- B27 No committed test composes the Production Dependencies into\n743|  Acquire: AFG reaches the adapter and bind gates only through\n744|  caller-injected implementations (the 19 Table C U2c cells). The\n745|  injection seam is first-leaf-owned; Production wiring is\n746|  unit-pinned (TestProductionWiresDependencies). Owner: composition\n747|  test, sibling scope.\n748|- B28 The backend command-error wrap is unmeasured at PFX (no\n749|  backend test stages a refused build; the builder rows pin the\n750|  refused shapes at CMD). Owner: this leaf; retest with a\n751|  refused-build backend test.\n752|- B29 The close-confirm poll deadline is pinned for past-deadline\n753|  at PFX via direct staging; the exact-boundary member and\n754|  dispatch-level staging are unmeasured (the fake runner advances\n755|  no time). Owner: hardening.\n756|- B30 The OSRunner exit/transport/argv mappings are total functions\n757|  over uncoded inputs with no refused class to admit a member of;\n758|  tests pin them including real-exec scrub, stderr-capture, and\n759|  signal-death integrations. The signal-death arm (a killed child\n760|  errors instead of reporting -1 data) is a refused class and\n761|  carries its own narrowing row; the remaining mappings stay total.\n762|  Owner: this leaf.\n763|- B31 The custody root-ownership arm is untested and singleton: the\n764|  ownership seam stages leaf-first (the leaf refuses before the\n765|  root arm runs), and a truly foreign root needs privilege. Owner:\n766|  hardening with a privileged stage or a root-level seam.\n767|- B32 The leaf-delegation wiring is measured at CUS (wrong-leaf\n768|  mutants are observable only on compliant roots); the absence\n769|  propagation through the six dispatch paths, the prober, and the\n770|  spawner is pinned by absence tests without a row. Owner: this\n771|  leaf.\n772|- B33 The wrapper safe-boundary signal step is unimplemented in the\n773|  landed wrapper: the boundary entry waits blocking on\n774|  `ax-boundary-<generation>` for the wrapper's `wait-for -S`, and\n775|  the wrapper never signals today, so boundary waits time out with\n776|  the coded quiesce_timeout (fail closed, never a faked proof)\n777|  until the signal step lands. The wait vector, the proof-kind\n778|  binding, the provider-row context, and the timeout are this\n779|  leaf's and fully driven; the signal emission is the wrapper's.\n780|  Owner: the wrapper (`ax pane`) task; retest the full\n781|  quiesce-boundary-stop flow when the signal lands.\n782|- B34 A crash between the mutation-receipt commit and the operation\n783|  outcome record re-observes the report time on retry: the effect\n784|  never re-runs and the evidence never changes, but the reported\n785|  closure/boundary time renders from the retry clock instead of\n786|  the original one. Sequential retries without a crash replay\n787|  identical times. Owner: this leaf; closing the window needs the\n788|  outcome inside the engine-owned receipt.\n789|- B35 The absence stderr markers are verified against tmux 3.6a\n790|  (`can't find session`, `can't find window`, and the\n791|  no-such-socket connect error); any other version's\n792|  absence-shaped stderr fails closed to unknown. Owner: this leaf;\n793|  re-verify the marker set when the tmux floor version moves.\n794|- B36 The Execute dispatch and the ExecuteWrapperRestore entry pin\n795|  their dependency singletons without per-arm narrowing rows: a\n796|  nil lifecycle or a nil Runner, Receipts, Bindings, Attach,\n797|  States, CurrentLease, CurrentGeneration, or Now refuses\n798|  protocol-error before any decision or effect. Admitting one nil\n799|  arm is deleting the check. Owner: this leaf; retest if any site\n800|  grows a second refused member.\n801|- B37 Unassigned (numbering gap; reserved).\n802|- B38 Union-rival ambiguity is unmodeled at the after-restore\n803|  composition: the entry decides over the single refreshed or\n804|  local winner, and a refresh adapter that observes rivals must\n805|  surface them as refresh failure so the entry parks unverified.\n806|  Owner: the mesh-refresh composition; retest when rivals are\n807|  modeled.\n808|- B39 Reachable-undriven: the entry reaches the gate but the\n809|  committed tests carry post-gate values only, so the refused\n810|  direction is undriven at that entry; the narrowed direction is\n811|  measured at the listed entry (\"M at ...\"). Formerly claimed\n812|  unreachable as U2b; stated as a bound now. Owner: this leaf;\n813|  drive a direction to move its cell to M.\n814|\n815|Carried bounds (first-leaf statements dispositioned by this leaf).\n816|B9 adapter split is discharged: the production exec, dial, probe,\n817|and spawn adapters ship (exec.go, probe.go, backend.go) and\n818|Production wires them into Dependencies; the residual is the\n819|uncomposed wiring (B27). B16 nested invocation is decided: lifecycle\n820|entries take no Ambient input, so nesting cannot collide through\n821|them (row 90); the Acquire-level over-strict nested refusal stands\n822|unchanged as first-leaf-owned. B18 sun_path is decided: strict-below\n823|per platform, counted in bytes (row 66). B19/B20 bind step is built:\n824|CheckSocketCustody enforces placement, leaf delegation, root,\n825|ancestors, and socket kind (rows 67-70); the bind step refuses\n826|intermediate symlinks through no-follow opens, which is stricter\n827|than the B11 Acquire rule it stands beside. The rev7 P3-A fresh-decoy\n828|foreground attach wiring is closed: TestAcquireForegroundRefusesEveryCatalogDecoyRunning\n829|refuses every catalog-derived decoy alone and together on the\n830|foreground running path with a spawn spy silent on every member, and\n831|the attach attestation cells carry N-attach-attestation-decoy. New\n832|bounds this revision: B33 states the unimplemented wrapper boundary\n833|signal (fail-closed timeout until it lands), B34 the receipt/outcome\n834|crash window, B35 the tmux-version marker set, B36 the dependency\n835|singletons, B38 the unmodeled union rivals, and B39 the\n836|reachable-undriven reclass (B37 unassigned).","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
