 those 18 cells read U2c.\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\\nsub(\\\"\\\"\\\"Table D: new gates × new entries (119 × 21 = 2499 cells; 167 M, 152\\nB, 2180 U; counts verified by script over the table).\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Table D: new gates × new entries (129 × 21 = 2709 cells; 178 M, 177\\nB, 2354 U; counts verified by script over the table).\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\\nsub(\\\"propagation elsewhere); leafwiring CUS 2 sites; rootwrite CUS 1 /\\\\nEXC 1 / EXS 1 / EXR 1 / shared EachOperation row (EXA, EXE, EXT);\\\",\\n    \\\"propagation elsewhere); leafwiring CUS 2 sites; rootwrite CUS 1 /\\\\nEXC 1 / EXS 1 / EXR 1 / SPW 1 / shared EachOperation row (EXA, EXE, EXT);\\\")\\n\\nsub(\\\"\\\"\\\"statusnegative EXS 1 each + statusmatch LOOK 1; prioragree EXR 4\\ntests, 3 rows; succession EXR 3 members; execdeps 6 EX pinned\\n(B36); Table B verify 9 new-entry sides shared 1, server EXA 1 (its\\nother sides are first-leaf symmetry).\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"statusnegative EXS 1 each + statusmatch LOOK 1; prioragree EXR 4\\ntests, 3 rows; succession EXR 3 members; execdeps 6 EX pinned\\n(B36); Table B verify 9 new-entry sides shared 1, server EXA 1 (its\\nother sides are first-leaf symmetry). Revision-4 gates:\\nquiescerecord/boundaryrecord single-sided at EXE;\\nbarrierquiesce/barrierboundary/barrierdecode/barrierempty\\nsingle-sided at EXA (same entry as the quiescegate memory arm, whose\\nrow points at them); attachedexit/foreignrow/panesexit single\\nmeasured side at EXS (EXT/EXR B39 via the resume reconcile);\\nargvnul single-sided at OSR (mirrors osrun: no committed Execute\\ncomposition injects OSRunner).\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\\nsub(\\\"\\\"\\\"Ratio: 227 measured of 5576 (50+10+167 M across Tables A/B/D;\\nTable C all U); 156 bound; 4193 unreachable with reasons. Every\\ndriven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 27\\ndriven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\\nB29 poll past-deadline, B32 propagation, B36 singleton deps) and\\n125 named undriven gaps (B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch\\nside, and the 117 B39 reachable-undriven cells), each with its\\nowner below. (Table A's 4 B15 guard-name arms are bound outside\\nthis split.)\\\"\\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Ratio: 238 measured of 4896 (50+10+178 M across Tables A/B/D;\\nTable C all U); 181 bound; 4477 unreachable with reasons. Every\\ndriven refusal direction is measured except the bound cells: 27\\ndriven but rowless (B22 singletons/forks, B23 normalized details,\\nB29 poll past-deadline, B32 propagation, B36 singleton deps) and\\n150 named undriven gaps (B24/B25/B26/B28/B31 cells, B29 dispatch\\nside, and the 142 B39 reachable-undriven cells), each with its\\nowner below. (Table A's 4 B15 guard-name arms are bound outside\\nthis split.)\\\"\\\"\\\")\\n\\np.write_text(raw)\\nprint(\\\"headers updated\\\")\\nPYEOF\\npython3 /tmp/census_count.py internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md\",\n  \"description\": \"Update census headers with fixed anchor\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"headers updated\\nTable A: 24x11=264 cells; M=50 B=4 U=210 ???=0 detail={'M': 50, 'U2': 133, 'U1': 77, 'B': 4}\\nTable B: 24x21=504 cells; M=10 B=0 U=494 ???=0 detail={'U2a': 494, 'M': 10}\\nTable D: 129x21=2709 cells; M=178 B=177 U=2354 ???=0 detail={'B': 177, 'U1': 2124, 'M': 178, 'U2a': 228, 'U3': 2}\\nTOTAL A+B+D: 3477 cells; M=238 B=181 U=3058\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 343,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 86,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
