{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000df4f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c7e8-b0ce-7b51-a856-c1e5aeba35b8"},"sequence":3586,"recorded_at":1780531400007167,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c801-2698-76c1-9a0f-961df0fba866"},"task_id":"01a0c801-2698-76c1-9a0f-961df0fba866","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c801-2698-76c1-9a0f-961df0fba866","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-102-1\",\n  \"command\": \"M=/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board/.resources/TASK-260830-1c28dz/TASK-260830-1c28dz_conformance-matrix.md; sed -n '1,31p' $M; echo ===; task-board resource add --help 2>&1 | head -25\",\n  \"description\": \"Read matrix header and resource add usage\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"# Conformance matrix — TASK-260830-1c28dz (implement-tmux-lifecycle-operations)\\n\\nDoD verdict: all acceptance criteria driven (rows 59-92 of\\n`internal/tmuxserver/TRACEABILITY.md`, 34 of 34 new rows green,\\nplus termbind row 67 for the reboot-successor mint), zero\\nreal-tmux witnesses by the determinism design (bound B1,\\ncarried), 159 second-leaf narrowing mutants KILLED plus the\\nshared harmless control SURVIVED (235/235 tmuxserver rows and\\n40/40 termbind rows as expected), gate x entry census 227\\nmeasured of 5576 with 156 stated bounds and 125 named undriven\\ngaps, after-restore outcome grid (Table E, 13 outcomes) green,\\nvalidation suite green firsthand (see the evidence tarball).\\nNo capability or CLI claims: this leaf ships library behavior\\nonly, exercised through `go test` as below.\\n\\nScope: §4.2 production adapters (exec, dial, probe, spawn), the\\nB18/B19/B20 socket bind step, and the §4.C lifecycle operations\\ncreate, attach, status, quiesce-input, wait-safe-boundary,\\nrequest-stop, terminate-stale, restore with receipt discipline,\\ntamper evidence, the AX-side state memory, the termbind\\nreboot-successor mint, and the after-restore wrapper\\ncomposition (refresh-before-decide with lapsed-grant remote\\noffer). Landed code is composed, never forked: terminstance\\nengine/receipts/results, terminalbackend\\nvocabulary/transitions/conformance, termbind and axpane stores,\\nfencing gates, sessrepo summaries, scalar and environ grammars,\\nsecprim argv guard, and the first-leaf custody and readiness\\ngates are called as-is; the only touched landed files are the\\nerror-code registry (new codes), the ownership seam (test\\nhook), and the mutant harnesses (new rows).\\n\\n===\\nAttach a new file resource to a board element.\\n\\nSOURCE may be:\\n  - a local filesystem path\\n  - a file:// URL\\n  - an http:// or https:// URL\\n\\nExamples:\\n  task-board resource add TASK-260311-abc ./screenshot.png --type precondition\\n  task-board resource add TASK-260311-abc file:///tmp/report.pdf --name ui-report.pdf\\n  task-board resource add TASK-260311-abc ./report.md --name reports/review/report.md\\n  task-board resource add TASK-260311-abc https://example.com/spec.pdf --type outcome\\n\\nUsage:\\n  task-board resource add <ELEMENT-ID> <SOURCE> [flags]\\n\\nFlags:\\n  -d, --description string   Optional one-line description\\n  -h, --help                 help for add\\n      --name string          Override stored resource filename\\n      --type string          Resource type: precondition or outcome (default \\\"outcome\\\")\\n\\nGlobal Flags:\\n      --board-dir string         Path to the board directory (overrides TASK_BOARD_DIR and config local.board_dir) (default \\\".task-board\\\")\\n      --context-profile string   Agent context profile override: full or lite\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2720,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 680,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
