{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000ee6f","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0c7e8-b0ce-7b51-a856-c1e5aeba35b8"},"sequence":5522,"recorded_at":1780531400011039,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"1e747257-7dba-4be5-8162-7ca370e28419"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0c816-c8d4-70b0-9876-c896d155fb1a"},"task_id":"01a0c816-c8d4-70b0-9876-c896d155fb1a","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0c816-c8d4-70b0-9876-c896d155fb1a","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-172-1\",\n  \"command\": \"git diff HEAD -- README.md | head -50; echo \\\"=====LOGBOOK=====\\\"; git diff HEAD -- LOGBOOK.md | head -40\",\n  \"description\": \"Review leaf README and LOGBOOK additions\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"diff --git a/README.md b/README.md\\nindex b5bef97..23afed5 100644\\n--- a/README.md\\n+++ b/README.md\\n@@ -2397,7 +2397,27 @@ composed only with generation equality: a missing realm row or a\\n stale-generation admission refuses, so a cached observation replayed as\\n live authorizes nothing. Every broker, server, and spawner interaction\\n runs through injected dependencies, so the suite passes with no tmux\\n-process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request.\\n+process anywhere; native Windows refuses every request. Lifecycle\\n+operations — create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop,\\n+stale termination, restore — run through structured argv builders over\\n+the dedicated socket: `Execute` admits exactly the eight operations\\n+and refuses unknown ones, the exec adapter reconstructs the exact\\n+`tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation and refuses\\n+forged binaries, flag injection, and ambient socket discovery, and\\n+the probed socket generation is bound (B18-B20) before any execution.\\n+Bodies are pure argv builders whose stable pane entrypoint stays\\n+`ax pane SESSION_ID`; effects run through the landed terminstance\\n+engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and\\n+AX-side state memory for reconciliation, while attach, terminate, and\\n+restore mirror the landed backend, fencing, and axpane gates. Quiesce\\n+cuts operator input by locking then detaching every attached client\\n+and refusing new input-authorized attaches at the entry (read-only\\n+observation stays); the boundary waits blocking for the wrapper\\n+signal with the proof kind bound into its evidence; probes prove\\n+absence only from marked tmux stderr and read every other failure as\\n+unknown. Every mutating operation replays the identical request\\n+idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before\\n+resuming.\\n \\n Run the focused tests and coverage with:\\n \\n@@ -2406,7 +2426,7 @@ go test ./internal/tmuxserver -count=1\\n go test ./internal/tmuxserver -cover -count=1\\n ```\\n \\n-Run the narrowing battery (73 narrowing mutants, two supplementary\\n+Run the narrowing battery (207 narrowing mutants, two supplementary\\n additive rows, plus one harmless control) with:\\n \\n ```bash\\n@@ -2418,7 +2438,9 @@ through the production entry point, restores the file from backup, and\\n reports per-row verdicts with subprocess exits; `AX_MUTANT_VERBOSE=1`\\n additionally prints the raw per-plant logs, and `--log-dir` captures one\\n raw log per plant. Task validation logs and mutation artifacts are\\n-attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`. The package adds no `ax` command, no\\n+attached to `TASK-260830-35urbp`, with the lifecycle battery and its\\n+raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. The package adds\\n+no `ax` command, no\\n=====LOGBOOK=====\\ndiff --git a/LOGBOOK.md b/LOGBOOK.md\\nindex ff58edc..76c445e 100644\\n--- a/LOGBOOK.md\\n+++ b/LOGBOOK.md\\n@@ -23,6 +23,15 @@\\n - VALIDATION: the fresh configured run is recorded under `.temp/BUG-260917-3lddu0/validation-rev3/`; all 30 configured commands exited 0. `task-board validate` reported 179 existing `MISSING_ACTIVITY` diagnostics and exited 0; scoped tracecheck §2.4 exited 0 and §5.3 exited 1 as the expected 7/8 refusal.\\n - HANDOFF: importer outcomes and tracecheck logs are task-scoped; the candidate remains UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree for snapshot handoff.\\n \\n+## 2026-09-22\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz — tmux lifecycle operations via structured commands (initial producer delivery)\\n+\\n+- SHIPPED the second `tmuxserver` leaf: `Execute` admits exactly the eight lifecycle operations (create, attach, status, quiesce, safe-boundary, stop, stale termination, restore) and refuses unknown ones; the exec adapter reconstructs the exact `tmux -S <socket> <subcommand>` vector per operation (forged binaries, flag injection, ambient discovery all refuse); the probed socket generation binds before execution (B18-B20); bodies are pure argv builders with the stable `ax pane SESSION_ID` entrypoint; effects run through the landed terminstance engine with strict per-operation deadlines, generation rechecks, and AX-side state memory, while attach/terminate/restore mirror the landed backend/fencing/axpane gates. Every mutating operation replays idempotently; uncertain receipts reconcile through status before resuming.\\n+- Battery: 173 narrowing + 2 additive KILLED + control SURVIVED (100 new second-leaf narrowing rows with per-arm killers; first leaf's 76 rows still green, shared control). AC: 33 of 33 rows (59-91) driven through production entries by named tests. Second-leaf census: Table B 24×21 (10 measured), Table C 90×11 (all unreachable), Table D 90×21 (108 measured), every measured cell with a named test plus an admitting narrowing row; singleton arms bound by B22, engine-normalized status by B23.\\n+- Full 30-command suite green firsthand on the frozen tree (gofmt, build, vet, full suite, race gate, cover, all fuzz gates, tracecheck, cataloggen, linux/windows builds, JSON check, board validate, diff check, windows vet); OUTCOME-keyed base-vs-candidate importer comparison clean (base 82 PASS retained, zero regressions). Evidence tarball with raw per-plant logs attached to `TASK-260830-1c28dz`. Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree.\\n+- Process note: a full-suite cover gate failed while the mutant harness was still running in the same tree — the cover run compiled against a planted mutant. Re-ran clean after the harness exited 0. Never run `go test` concurrently with the harness in one worktree.\\n+\\n ## 2026-09-21\\n \\n ### BUG-260917-2fwf8e — fencing direction must beat lapsed-grant refusal\\n@@ -2633,3 +2642,15 @@ assertion here rather than a brittle one.\\n - COVERAGE RATIO: 19 of 21 enumerated production acceptance rows are driven by named production-entry tests. The two stated bounds remain: Windows runtime DACL execution is not available on this Darwin runner, and this repository has no export/replication consumer surface for host-trust secret exclusion. No claim is made for either bound.\\n - VALIDATION: grouped full suite `go test -count=1 -v` A/B/C/D all exit 0 across all 26 packages; grouped full coverage A/B/C/D all exit 0 (`config 93.5%`, `hosttrust 77.9%`, `peeridentity 97.5%`); scoped hosttrust/config/peeridentity tests, scoped vet, native/Linux-arm64/Windows-amd64 builds, Windows test compilation, `go mod tidy -diff`, and `git diff --check` are green. Logs and package inventory are in `.temp/TASK-260909-2ez769/`.\\n - STATUS: ready for review; worktree remains intentionally UNCOMMITTED for Story handoff snapshot.\\n+\\n+### TASK-260830-1c28dz rework rev2 — rev1 CHANGES REQUESTED repaired on checkpoint 1ba06e9\\n+- SCOPE: second leaf of STORY-260830-2t4g7i, tmux lifecycle operations. All five P1 + two P2 closed in `internal/tmuxserver`; trunk unmoved, no rebase. Only touched landed files: error-code registry (new codes